1
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:09,913
Hi.

2
00:00:09,943 --> 00:00:11,344
Let me ask you something.

3
00:00:11,374 --> 00:00:13,234
Is your phone ringing again and again?

4
00:00:13,264 --> 00:00:15,312
Forty, maybe fifty calls a day?

5
00:00:15,342 --> 00:00:19,577
Messages that say the police are coming, or that someone will come to your home?

6
00:00:19,607 --> 00:00:21,837
Maybe your family is getting calls too.

7
00:00:22,237 --> 00:00:24,264
If yes, first, take a deep breath.

8
00:00:24,294 --> 00:00:25,338
You're not alone.

9
00:00:25,368 --> 00:00:27,602
This happens to lakhs of people in India.

10
00:00:28,002 --> 00:00:30,370
It usually starts with something you didn't plan.

11
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:31,849
Maybe someone got sick.

12
00:00:31,879 --> 00:00:33,424
Maybe you lost your job.

13
00:00:33,454 --> 00:00:35,196
Maybe your business slowed down.

14
00:00:35,226 --> 00:00:39,428
You miss one payment, and within days, it feels like everyone is after you.

15
00:00:39,828 --> 00:00:41,896
And when we panic, we make mistakes.

16
00:00:41,926 --> 00:00:43,690
People take loans from apps.

17
00:00:43,720 --> 00:00:45,228
They sell family gold.

18
00:00:45,258 --> 00:00:46,935
Just to pay the 'Minimum Due'.

19
00:00:46,965 --> 00:00:48,466
But here's the sad part.

20
00:00:48,496 --> 00:00:51,032
Most of that money just goes into interest.

21
00:00:51,432 --> 00:00:53,078
So listen to me carefully.

22
00:00:53,108 --> 00:00:56,012
Debt is a financial event, not a moral crime.

23
00:00:56,042 --> 00:00:57,128
You didn't steal.

24
00:00:57,158 --> 00:00:58,261
You didn't cheat.

25
00:00:58,291 --> 00:00:59,893
You just hit a money problem.

26
00:00:59,923 --> 00:01:03,095
That does not make you a bad person, and it's not a crime.

27
00:01:03,495 --> 00:01:05,229
Now, let me show you something.

28
00:01:05,259 --> 00:01:06,612
Look at the business side.

29
00:01:06,642 --> 00:01:12,292
Why do credit cards charge around 42% to 48% interest every year?

30
00:01:12,322 --> 00:01:15,018
Because the bank took nothing from you as security.

31
00:01:15,048 --> 00:01:16,040
No house.

32
00:01:16,070 --> 00:01:17,050
No gold.

33
00:01:17,080 --> 00:01:18,059
No land.

34
00:01:18,089 --> 00:01:20,289
They know some people won't be able to pay.

35
00:01:20,319 --> 00:01:22,943
That big interest is how they cover that risk.

36
00:01:22,973 --> 00:01:24,612
They planned for it from day one.

37
00:01:25,012 --> 00:01:26,597
And remember the Golden Rule.

38
00:01:26,627 --> 00:01:28,173
Your family comes first.

39
00:01:28,203 --> 00:01:30,318
Food, medicine, rent, school fees.

40
00:01:30,348 --> 00:01:33,725
All of that takes absolute priority over paying the bank.

41
00:01:33,755 --> 00:01:36,268
Never starve your family to pay a card bill.

42
00:01:36,298 --> 00:01:37,098
Okay?

43
00:01:37,128 --> 00:01:39,554
Let's fix this the right way, step by step.

44
00:01:39,584 --> 00:01:42,212
And step one is knowing what the law really says.

45
00:01:46,233 --> 00:01:47,811
So, debt is not a crime.

46
00:01:47,841 --> 00:01:51,990
But the recovery agents will try very hard to make you feel like a criminal.

47
00:01:52,020 --> 00:01:53,904
Let's see what the law actually says.

48
00:01:54,304 --> 00:01:56,140
What's the biggest weapon they use?

49
00:01:56,170 --> 00:01:56,885
Fear.

50
00:01:56,915 --> 00:02:01,567
They'll shout things like 'Section 420', 'criminal case', 'police will come'.

51
00:02:01,597 --> 00:02:02,690
Scary, right?

52
00:02:03,090 --> 00:02:08,225
A credit card or a personal loan is just a contract, an agreement between you and the

53
00:02:07,975 --> 00:02:08,497
bank.

54
00:02:08,527 --> 00:02:12,028
It comes under the Indian Contract Act of 1872.

55
00:02:12,058 --> 00:02:16,239
If you can't pay because you really ran out of money, that's usually a civil matter.

56
00:02:16,269 --> 00:02:17,554
Not a criminal one.

57
00:02:17,954 --> 00:02:19,823
So what can the bank actually do?

58
00:02:19,853 --> 00:02:21,626
Their options are civil ones.

59
00:02:21,656 --> 00:02:27,309
They can file a money case in civil court, called a summary suit under Order 37 of the

60
00:02:27,059 --> 00:02:28,006
CPC.

61
00:02:28,036 --> 00:02:30,352
They can take it to a National Lok Adalat.

62
00:02:30,382 --> 00:02:32,875
Or they can file a normal recovery case.

63
00:02:32,905 --> 00:02:34,801
But here's the most important part.

64
00:02:34,831 --> 00:02:39,955
Indian criminal law has no rule to arrest you just because you honestly couldn't pay.

65
00:02:40,355 --> 00:02:41,499
What about cheating?

66
00:02:41,529 --> 00:02:46,302
The Supreme Court has said, in established judgments, that cheating means you planned

67
00:02:46,052 --> 00:02:48,196
to fool the bank from the very first day.

68
00:02:48,226 --> 00:02:52,927
If you maintained a normal payment record before your problems started, that shows you

69
00:02:52,677 --> 00:02:53,858
had no such plan.

70
00:02:53,888 --> 00:02:56,683
So a cheating case is very unlikely to stand.

71
00:02:57,083 --> 00:02:58,169
And the police?

72
00:02:58,199 --> 00:03:00,689
Police are not the bank's recovery agents.

73
00:03:00,719 --> 00:03:05,402
An unpaid card bill is not a police matter, and police usually shouldn't call you to

74
00:03:05,152 --> 00:03:06,246
the station for it.

75
00:03:06,276 --> 00:03:11,180
You may hear about Section 138 or Section 25 PSSA.

76
00:03:11,210 --> 00:03:14,232
Those are for bounced cheques and failed auto-debits.

77
00:03:14,262 --> 00:03:17,404
Pure credit card defaults usually don't come under them.

78
00:03:21,433 --> 00:03:22,230
Okay.

79
00:03:22,260 --> 00:03:26,121
So the law is on your side, and the police are not the bank's agents.

80
00:03:26,151 --> 00:03:28,825
But what if you owe money to not one bank, but many?

81
00:03:29,225 --> 00:03:30,422
And here's the fear.

82
00:03:30,452 --> 00:03:34,241
What if all the banks join together and file one big case against you?

83
00:03:34,641 --> 00:03:35,515
Relax.

84
00:03:35,545 --> 00:03:36,933
It doesn't work like that.

85
00:03:36,963 --> 00:03:40,153
Every card is a separate agreement with a separate company.

86
00:03:40,183 --> 00:03:43,159
SBI Card cannot join with ICICI.

87
00:03:43,189 --> 00:03:45,261
Axis cannot share costs with Kotak.

88
00:03:45,291 --> 00:03:49,863
Each bank must hire its own lawyer, pay its own court fees, and fight its own case.

89
00:03:50,263 --> 00:03:51,881
And that's expensive for them.

90
00:03:51,911 --> 00:03:52,972
Let me show you.

91
00:03:53,002 --> 00:03:55,569
Look at how recovery works for different amounts.

92
00:03:55,599 --> 00:04:00,330
For small amounts, under fifteen thousand, or even up to fifty thousand,

93
00:04:00,080 --> 00:04:03,353
banks mostly just use computer calls and call centres.

94
00:04:03,383 --> 00:04:04,072
Why?

95
00:04:04,102 --> 00:04:08,846
Filing a civil suit can cost a bank fifteen to thirty-five thousand rupees.

96
00:04:08,876 --> 00:04:10,111
Now think about it.

97
00:04:10,141 --> 00:04:13,542
Would you spend twenty-five thousand to get back fifteen thousand?

98
00:04:13,572 --> 00:04:14,541
No, right?

99
00:04:14,571 --> 00:04:16,131
Banks usually won't either.

100
00:04:16,531 --> 00:04:20,661
Even in high tiers above one lakh, card cases rarely go to court.

101
00:04:20,691 --> 00:04:21,843
Courts are slow.

102
00:04:21,873 --> 00:04:23,227
Cases take years.

103
00:04:23,257 --> 00:04:28,317
That's why compromise settlements, often through Lok Adalat, are usually the easiest

104
00:04:28,067 --> 00:04:29,356
way out for the bank.

105
00:04:33,367 --> 00:04:35,916
So banks think about cost before they chase you.

106
00:04:35,946 --> 00:04:39,926
Now let's look at the other side of the money, the big number on your statement.

107
00:04:40,326 --> 00:04:41,612
Have you noticed this?

108
00:04:41,642 --> 00:04:43,011
Your card is blocked.

109
00:04:43,041 --> 00:04:44,933
You haven't spent even one rupee.

110
00:04:44,963 --> 00:04:46,861
But the amount keeps going up and up.

111
00:04:46,891 --> 00:04:48,013
Strange, right?

112
00:04:48,043 --> 00:04:49,789
I call this Phantom Accounting.

113
00:04:50,189 --> 00:04:51,483
Here's what happens.

114
00:04:51,513 --> 00:04:56,187
The moment you miss payments, the bank's computer starts adding charges by itself.

115
00:04:56,217 --> 00:04:58,145
First, late payment charges.

116
00:04:58,175 --> 00:05:03,491
Then revolving finance charges, which means interest, up to forty-eight percent a year.

117
00:05:03,521 --> 00:05:05,178
Then over-limit charges.

118
00:05:05,208 --> 00:05:06,734
And here's the funny part.

119
00:05:06,764 --> 00:05:09,507
You only crossed your limit because of their own fees!

120
00:05:09,537 --> 00:05:13,746
And on top of everything, eighteen percent GST on every charge.

121
00:05:14,146 --> 00:05:19,003
In six months, a one-lakh rupee debt can grow to almost one lakh forty thousand.

122
00:05:19,033 --> 00:05:22,777
Leave it for a year, and it can cross one lakh sixty-five thousand.

123
00:05:22,807 --> 00:05:25,857
The bank knows it will never collect most of that extra.

124
00:05:26,257 --> 00:05:27,464
Now, good news.

125
00:05:27,494 --> 00:05:32,257
Under the RBI Framework for Compromise Settlements and Technical Write-offs,

126
00:05:32,007 --> 00:05:37,540
when you do a proper One-Time Settlement, these penalties and extra interest may be waived,

127
00:05:37,290 --> 00:05:38,420
often completely.

128
00:05:38,450 --> 00:05:41,705
So always try to settle based on what you actually spent.

129
00:05:41,735 --> 00:05:43,685
Not the big number on your statement.

130
00:05:47,700 --> 00:05:50,264
So most of that scary balance is just fees.

131
00:05:50,293 --> 00:05:54,446
But before we talk about settling anything, there's one thing you must do first.

132
00:05:54,846 --> 00:05:58,149
Before you answer even one recovery call, do this first.

133
00:05:58,179 --> 00:05:59,791
Protect your family's money.

134
00:05:59,821 --> 00:06:01,324
This is very important.

135
00:06:01,724 --> 00:06:08,176
Under Section 171 of the Indian Contract Act, and the rules in most bank agreements,

136
00:06:07,926 --> 00:06:10,436
banks have something called the Right of Set-Off.

137
00:06:10,466 --> 00:06:11,837
What does that mean for you?

138
00:06:11,867 --> 00:06:13,310
Let me explain simply.

139
00:06:13,340 --> 00:06:18,350
If you have an unpaid card with Bank A, and your salary also comes into your savings

140
00:06:18,100 --> 00:06:22,287
account at Bank A, the bank may sweep your savings balance to zero.

141
00:06:22,317 --> 00:06:23,682
They don't need a court order.

142
00:06:23,712 --> 00:06:27,611
Imagine waking up on salary day and finding nothing in your account.

143
00:06:28,011 --> 00:06:29,522
So here's your first move.

144
00:06:29,552 --> 00:06:34,051
Move your salary, your savings, and your family's money to a totally clean bank.

145
00:06:34,081 --> 00:06:37,904
A bank where you have no loan, no credit card, and no overdraft.

146
00:06:37,934 --> 00:06:40,096
One that has nothing it can take from you.

147
00:06:40,496 --> 00:06:43,781
And keep every bank where you owe money at a zero balance.

148
00:06:43,811 --> 00:06:49,452
Your family's groceries, medicines, and home loan EMI always come before credit card

149
00:06:49,202 --> 00:06:49,739
bills.

150
00:06:53,767 --> 00:06:54,478
Good.

151
00:06:54,508 --> 00:06:56,075
Your salary is safe now.

152
00:06:56,105 --> 00:06:59,305
The next question is, how should you deal with the bank itself?

153
00:06:59,705 --> 00:07:04,198
Many people think, 'I'll just switch off my phone and disappear.' Please don't do that.

154
00:07:04,228 --> 00:07:08,711
If you go totally silent, the bank's system may mark you as 'Skip or Absconding'.

155
00:07:08,741 --> 00:07:10,603
That means they think you ran away.

156
00:07:10,633 --> 00:07:14,481
And then they start calling your relatives, your friends, even your office.

157
00:07:14,881 --> 00:07:16,677
Instead, build a paper trail.

158
00:07:16,707 --> 00:07:20,161
Send a proper email to the bank's Principal Nodal Officer.

159
00:07:20,191 --> 00:07:23,268
That's the top person who handles complaints in the bank.

160
00:07:23,668 --> 00:07:26,164
In that email, write four simple things.

161
00:07:26,194 --> 00:07:27,980
First, explain what happened.

162
00:07:28,010 --> 00:07:30,252
Illness, job loss, whatever it was.

163
00:07:30,282 --> 00:07:33,751
Second, declare that you are reachable, and you're not running away.

164
00:07:33,781 --> 00:07:37,895
Third, request that because of the stress, they talk to you only in writing,

165
00:07:37,645 --> 00:07:38,440
by email.

166
00:07:38,470 --> 00:07:43,086
Fourth, state that you want to settle with a proper One-Time Settlement once your money

167
00:07:42,836 --> 00:07:44,139
situation is better.

168
00:07:44,539 --> 00:07:46,832
The bank will reply with a reference number.

169
00:07:46,862 --> 00:07:47,890
Keep it safe.

170
00:07:47,920 --> 00:07:50,133
The Case Reference ID is your proof.

171
00:07:50,163 --> 00:07:51,870
It shows you acted honestly.

172
00:07:51,900 --> 00:07:54,539
It helps counter any claim of 'Willful Default'.

173
00:07:54,569 --> 00:07:56,603
And it helps you later at Lok Adalat.

174
00:08:00,633 --> 00:08:03,603
Now the bank has your email, and you have a paper trail.

175
00:08:03,633 --> 00:08:06,138
But the recovery agents won't stop right away.

176
00:08:06,168 --> 00:08:09,203
So let me show you their tricks, so they can't scare you anymore.

177
00:08:09,603 --> 00:08:12,625
Recovery agents often use the same few tricks.

178
00:08:12,655 --> 00:08:14,709
Once you know them, they stop working.

179
00:08:14,739 --> 00:08:15,474
Ready?

180
00:08:15,504 --> 00:08:16,918
Let's go one by one.

181
00:08:17,318 --> 00:08:20,167
Number One: the WhatsApp live location message.

182
00:08:20,197 --> 00:08:22,933
You get a text saying, 'Our team is near your house.

183
00:08:22,963 --> 00:08:25,458
Share your live location now.' Now think.

184
00:08:25,488 --> 00:08:29,906
If they really had your address, and the right to visit, why would they need your location?

185
00:08:29,936 --> 00:08:32,877
They may be sitting in a call center, just trying their luck.

186
00:08:32,907 --> 00:08:34,222
Just block the number.

187
00:08:34,622 --> 00:08:37,047
Number Two: the ghost visit SMS.

188
00:08:37,077 --> 00:08:39,046
'Our agent visited your house today.

189
00:08:39,076 --> 00:08:44,271
The door was locked.' This is often an automated script, a message sent to thousands

190
00:08:44,021 --> 00:08:45,693
of people at the same time.

191
00:08:45,723 --> 00:08:48,495
In many cases, nobody came to your door at all.

192
00:08:48,895 --> 00:08:50,747
Number Three: the tracking link.

193
00:08:50,777 --> 00:08:56,213
A message says, 'Click here to see your legal notice.' These are often ready-made messages

194
00:08:55,963 --> 00:08:57,756
with tracking tokens inside.

195
00:08:57,786 --> 00:09:02,181
If you click, they may see your IP and your phone details, and they know you're scared.

196
00:09:02,211 --> 00:09:07,313
Real court summons come properly, for example by registered post or through the court.

197
00:09:07,713 --> 00:09:09,947
And if someone actually knocks on your door?

198
00:09:09,977 --> 00:09:11,082
Don't let them in.

199
00:09:11,112 --> 00:09:14,304
Step outside and start a video recording on your phone.

200
00:09:14,334 --> 00:09:19,779
Politely ask for two documents: their ID card, and a letter from the bank for your account.

201
00:09:19,809 --> 00:09:24,529
If they cannot produce both, remind them of the RBI Fair Practices Code.

202
00:09:24,559 --> 00:09:27,348
And if you ever feel unsafe, dial 112.

203
00:09:27,378 --> 00:09:30,480
People without proper papers usually leave quickly.

204
00:09:34,500 --> 00:09:36,631
Those tricks mostly come by message.

205
00:09:36,661 --> 00:09:38,657
But what about the endless phone calls?

206
00:09:38,687 --> 00:09:40,106
Let's fix that next.

207
00:09:40,506 --> 00:09:41,909
Here's a simple truth.

208
00:09:41,939 --> 00:09:44,477
You can't win against a computer with emotions.

209
00:09:44,507 --> 00:09:48,676
Most of these calls come from a computer that dials numbers automatically.

210
00:09:48,706 --> 00:09:53,995
Every time you answer, even just to explain or argue, the system may mark your number

211
00:09:53,745 --> 00:09:54,438
as 'Active'.

212
00:09:54,468 --> 00:09:57,698
And an active number can get even more calls the next day.

213
00:09:58,098 --> 00:09:59,357
So what's the answer?

214
00:09:59,387 --> 00:10:01,600
The answer is mechanical silence.

215
00:10:01,630 --> 00:10:03,055
Split your phone lines.

216
00:10:03,085 --> 00:10:05,064
Keep work and family on SIM 1.

217
00:10:05,094 --> 00:10:09,542
On your card number, block the telemarketing series, like one-four-zero,

218
00:10:09,292 --> 00:10:10,857
and known call-centre numbers.

219
00:10:10,887 --> 00:10:13,667
And turn on 'Silence Unknown Callers' in WhatsApp.

220
00:10:13,697 --> 00:10:14,704
Easy, right?

221
00:10:15,104 --> 00:10:19,285
Outside agencies usually get your file for sixty to ninety days.

222
00:10:19,315 --> 00:10:23,992
When they get total silence, no clicks, and no small payments, their time may run out.

223
00:10:24,022 --> 00:10:28,330
The calls typically slow down, and the file may go back to the bank's own team.

224
00:10:32,333 --> 00:10:36,418
Once the calls are under control, you get something very valuable: time.

225
00:10:36,448 --> 00:10:39,543
And time matters, because banks settle on their own calendar.

226
00:10:39,943 --> 00:10:43,542
Once you understand this calendar, you'll see why patience matters.

227
00:10:43,942 --> 00:10:48,508
In the first thirty days, the bank calls your account Special Mention Account Zero.

228
00:10:48,538 --> 00:10:53,465
They still expect normal payment, and customer care usually can't offer any settlement.

229
00:10:53,865 --> 00:11:00,068
Between days thirty and ninety, called SMA-1 and SMA-2, your account may go to outside

230
00:10:59,818 --> 00:11:01,211
recovery agencies.

231
00:11:01,241 --> 00:11:03,258
This is when the calls are the worst.

232
00:11:03,288 --> 00:11:07,704
Banks may also offer to turn your card dues into a loan with EMIs.

233
00:11:07,734 --> 00:11:09,811
Think carefully before you say yes.

234
00:11:09,841 --> 00:11:13,039
It can start a brand new loan, with brand new problems.

235
00:11:13,439 --> 00:11:18,844
At ninety days, RBI rules say the bank must call your account a Non-Performing Asset.

236
00:11:18,874 --> 00:11:24,012
After that, the bank can't count your unpaid interest as income, and it must set aside

237
00:11:23,762 --> 00:11:25,543
its own money to cover the loss.

238
00:11:25,943 --> 00:11:30,729
Typically after about one hundred and eighty days, banks may write off the account from

239
00:11:30,479 --> 00:11:31,466
their main books.

240
00:11:31,496 --> 00:11:33,139
The loss is already counted.

241
00:11:33,169 --> 00:11:36,686
So any recovery effectively becomes extra profit for them.

242
00:11:36,716 --> 00:11:41,666
And this is often when real settlement offers, with bigger discounts, become possible.

243
00:11:45,667 --> 00:11:48,437
So now you know when banks become ready to settle.

244
00:11:48,468 --> 00:11:50,781
But not every bank behaves the same way.

245
00:11:51,181 --> 00:11:52,913
Every bank has its own style.

246
00:11:52,943 --> 00:11:57,073
What I'm sharing now comes from what many borrowers have commonly reported.

247
00:11:57,103 --> 00:12:00,362
So please treat these as rough patterns, not promises.

248
00:12:00,762 --> 00:12:07,049
SBI Card reportedly sends lots of automatic legal notices and has active recovery teams.

249
00:12:07,079 --> 00:12:11,300
Settlements around thirty to forty percent have been reported at Lok Adalat.

250
00:12:11,700 --> 00:12:16,354
HDFC Bank is known to use set-off, so keep your savings there at zero.

251
00:12:16,384 --> 00:12:20,664
Settlements around twenty-five to thirty-five percent have been reported,

252
00:12:20,414 --> 00:12:22,407
usually after about six months.

253
00:12:22,807 --> 00:12:28,605
ICICI Bank reportedly follows a more formal process, and often prefers settling through

254
00:12:28,355 --> 00:12:29,115
the courts.

255
00:12:29,515 --> 00:12:34,572
Axis, YES, and Kotak Mahindra reportedly send accounts to agencies quickly,

256
00:12:34,322 --> 00:12:39,217
and then to special settlement teams, where settlements around twenty-five to thirty-five

257
00:12:38,967 --> 00:12:40,568
percent have been reported.

258
00:12:40,968 --> 00:12:46,361
RBL Bank has reportedly given bigger discounts, around twenty to thirty percent,

259
00:12:46,111 --> 00:12:49,403
after a formal complaint to the Principal Nodal Officer.

260
00:12:49,803 --> 00:12:55,353
And IDFC FIRST Bank mostly works online, and reportedly settles in a clear,

261
00:12:55,103 --> 00:12:57,081
step-by-step way after write-off.

262
00:12:57,481 --> 00:12:59,340
We've covered eight big banks here.

263
00:12:59,370 --> 00:13:04,013
If your bank isn't on this list, tell me in the comments, and I'll cover it in a future

264
00:13:03,763 --> 00:13:04,367
video.

265
00:13:08,367 --> 00:13:12,765
Now that you know how different banks behave, let's talk about the settlement itself.

266
00:13:12,795 --> 00:13:14,403
How does it actually happen?

267
00:13:14,803 --> 00:13:18,394
Once your account is written off, there are usually two ways to settle.

268
00:13:18,424 --> 00:13:22,398
A National Lok Adalat, or a direct One-Time Settlement with the bank.

269
00:13:22,798 --> 00:13:28,343
National Lok Adalat is organized regularly by the National Legal Services Authority.

270
00:13:28,373 --> 00:13:32,389
Think of it as a friendly legal meeting, where both sides agree on a deal.

271
00:13:32,419 --> 00:13:36,474
An award passed at Lok Adalat is treated like a civil court decree.

272
00:13:36,504 --> 00:13:37,514
It is final.

273
00:13:37,544 --> 00:13:39,066
It binds both sides.

274
00:13:39,096 --> 00:13:41,106
And nobody can appeal against it.

275
00:13:41,506 --> 00:13:46,918
In compromise settlements, card balances have often been reported to settle at twenty-five

276
00:13:46,668 --> 00:13:49,472
to thirty-five percent of what you actually spent.

277
00:13:49,872 --> 00:13:50,766
But wait.

278
00:13:50,796 --> 00:13:53,663
Before you pay even one rupee, check four things.

279
00:13:53,693 --> 00:13:58,451
First: the settlement letter must be on the bank's official letterhead, signed by a bank

280
00:13:58,201 --> 00:13:58,814
officer.

281
00:13:58,844 --> 00:14:02,060
Never accept a letter only from a recovery agency.

282
00:14:02,090 --> 00:14:06,239
Second: the letter must show your exact card number and the settlement amount.

283
00:14:06,269 --> 00:14:10,964
Third: it must clearly say that after this payment, your account is fully closed,

284
00:14:10,714 --> 00:14:11,874
with zero balance.

285
00:14:11,904 --> 00:14:16,826
Fourth: it should promise a No Dues Certificate, usually within thirty to forty-five

286
00:14:16,576 --> 00:14:17,088
days.

287
00:14:17,488 --> 00:14:20,394
And when you pay, use only official bank channels.

288
00:14:20,424 --> 00:14:23,965
NEFT, RTGS, or the bank's own website.

289
00:14:23,995 --> 00:14:26,090
Never make cash payments to an agent.

290
00:14:26,120 --> 00:14:26,860
Never.

291
00:14:30,867 --> 00:14:33,449
Once you've settled, one big worry is left.

292
00:14:33,479 --> 00:14:34,999
What about my CIBIL score?

293
00:14:35,029 --> 00:14:36,664
Will I ever get a loan again?

294
00:14:37,064 --> 00:14:41,835
After you settle, your CIBIL report will show 'Settled', and your score will drop for

295
00:14:41,585 --> 00:14:42,331
some time.

296
00:14:42,361 --> 00:14:44,190
But is your financial life over?

297
00:14:44,220 --> 00:14:44,895
No!

298
00:14:44,925 --> 00:14:46,115
That's just a myth.

299
00:14:46,515 --> 00:14:52,022
Credit scoring models usually care most about how you behaved recently, especially the

300
00:14:51,772 --> 00:14:54,183
last twenty-four to thirty-six months.

301
00:14:54,583 --> 00:14:58,409
So once your settlements are done, and you have your No Dues Certificates,

302
00:14:58,159 --> 00:14:59,193
start rebuilding.

303
00:14:59,223 --> 00:15:00,160
Here's how.

304
00:15:00,190 --> 00:15:05,464
Open a small fixed deposit of twenty-five to fifty thousand rupees in a clean bank,

305
00:15:05,214 --> 00:15:08,225
and obtain an FD-backed Secured Credit Card on it.

306
00:15:08,255 --> 00:15:12,786
These cards usually don't need salary proof, because your deposit is the safety.

307
00:15:13,186 --> 00:15:17,257
Keep your monthly usage low, under fifteen to twenty percent of the limit.

308
00:15:17,287 --> 00:15:19,152
Use it only for small bills.

309
00:15:19,182 --> 00:15:21,991
And pay the full bill on time, every single month.

310
00:15:22,391 --> 00:15:25,998
Month after month, your report fills up with on-time payments.

311
00:15:26,028 --> 00:15:30,650
Within eighteen to twenty-four months, this good record can beat the old bad one,

312
00:15:30,400 --> 00:15:34,168
and may help bring your score back toward seven-hundred-and-fifty-plus.

313
00:15:34,568 --> 00:15:37,797
Debt is a difficult chapter, but it's not your whole story.

314
00:15:37,827 --> 00:15:39,416
Protect your family first.

315
00:15:39,446 --> 00:15:40,919
Trust the law, not fear.

316
00:15:40,949 --> 00:15:42,356
And settle with dignity.

317
00:15:46,367 --> 00:15:47,941
We've covered a lot today.

318
00:15:47,971 --> 00:15:50,626
So let's put it all together in one simple plan.

319
00:15:51,026 --> 00:15:52,975
Here's your simple eight-step plan.

320
00:15:53,375 --> 00:15:58,512
Step One: move your salary and savings to a clean bank, and keep your other bank balances

321
00:15:58,262 --> 00:15:58,995
at zero.

322
00:15:59,395 --> 00:16:04,218
Step Two: send a hardship email to the Principal Nodal Officer of each bank,

323
00:16:03,968 --> 00:16:05,415
and save your Case IDs.

324
00:16:05,815 --> 00:16:11,348
Step Three: turn on Silence Unknown Callers on WhatsApp, and block the auto-dialer numbers.

325
00:16:11,748 --> 00:16:16,320
Step Four: stop paying small amounts or Minimum Dues that only cover fees.

326
00:16:16,720 --> 00:16:18,839
Step Five: don't argue with callers.

327
00:16:18,869 --> 00:16:20,931
Ask the bank to talk to you in writing.

328
00:16:21,331 --> 00:16:22,867
Step Six: be patient.

329
00:16:22,897 --> 00:16:26,769
Real settlement talks usually start after the account is written off.

330
00:16:27,169 --> 00:16:32,888
Step Seven: do a proper One-Time Settlement, often reported around twenty-five to thirty-five

331
00:16:32,638 --> 00:16:33,263
percent.

332
00:16:33,294 --> 00:16:37,773
Check the official letter, pay the bank directly, and get your No Dues Certificate.

333
00:16:38,173 --> 00:16:43,252
And Step Eight: rebuild your credit with an FD-backed secured card, and bring your CIBIL

334
00:16:43,002 --> 00:16:45,805
score back toward seven-hundred-and-fifty-plus.

335
00:16:46,205 --> 00:16:49,145
Remember, you are not alone, and you are not a criminal.

336
00:16:49,175 --> 00:16:50,552
Take control today.

337
00:16:50,582 --> 00:16:52,241
The law protects your dignity.

338
00:16:52,271 --> 00:16:54,412
And here's something I haven't told you yet.

339
00:16:54,442 --> 00:16:56,643
I'm going through this myself, right now.

340
00:16:56,673 --> 00:17:01,894
In the next video, I'll show you my own case: exactly how I'm handling my banks,

341
00:17:01,644 --> 00:17:04,710
step by step, with real letters and real replies.

342
00:17:04,740 --> 00:17:07,445
So subscribe, and tap the bell, so you don't miss it.

343
00:17:07,475 --> 00:17:10,240
And if this helped you, share it with someone who needs it.
